# earlyoom — replaces systemd-oomd on this host.
#
# WHY NOT systemd-oomd: it kills whole cgroups, which assumes a desktop that
# puts each app in its own scope (GNOME/KDE do; sway does not). Here sway
# launches everything as a direct child, so sway, firefox, waybar, Xwayland,
# foot and tmux all share ONE flat session-N.scope. oomd's only choices were
# "kill the entire graphical session" or "kill a tmux scope holding a Claude
# Code session" — it could never reach the single runaway process. earlyoom
# works on processes by RSS, which is the right granularity for this layout.
#
# Thresholds are absolute (KiB), not percentages: this box has 124.9 GiB, so
# earlyoom's default -m 10,5 would sit at 12.5/6.2 GiB — far too late to be
# useful, and a lot of RAM to leave unused. Both the memory AND the swap
# condition must hold before earlyoom acts.
#   SIGTERM at <8 GiB available AND <8 GiB swap free   (8388608 KiB)
#   SIGKILL at <4 GiB available AND <4 GiB swap free   (4194304 KiB)
#
# --avoid protects what loses the session or the ability to recover from
# one. --prefer names the usual runaways. 'node' is deliberately NOT
# preferred: Claude Code sessions are node, and they are large without being
# the thing that ran away.
#
# TWO SYNTAX CONSTRAINTS, both easy to get wrong:
#   1. systemd expands $EARLYOOM_ARGS by splitting on whitespace and does
#      NOT strip quotes, so quoting a regex here passes the quote characters
#      through as part of the pattern. Never quote the regexes.
#   2. Following from that, the patterns must contain no spaces — '.' stands
#      in for a literal space below.
# Kills are logged to the journal: journalctl -u earlyoom
#
# Patterns match /proc/PID/comm, which the kernel TRUNCATES TO 15 CHARS.
# That is why it is 'Isolated.Web.Co' and 'systemd-journal', not the full
# names — matching the untruncated form would silently never fire.
EARLYOOM_ARGS=-r 3600 -M 8388608,4194304 -S 8388608,4194304 --avoid ^(sway|Xwayland|systemd|systemd-journal|dbus-broker|dbus-daemon|sshd|gpg-agent|tmux:.server|dockerd|containerd|swayidle|swaylock)$ --prefer ^(firefox|chromium|thunderbird|slack|java|Web.Content|Isolated.Web.Co)$
